    House style:

      * Second person for what you do, present indicative for what the app does.
      * Titles and choices are noun phrases with no full stop; summaries and
        dialog bodies are sentences with one; buttons are a verb or a noun.
      * A summary says what the setting does and what the other state does, in
        at most two sentences, with the unit and the default where there is one.
      * The machine at the other end is "the remote machine" and its screen is
        "the desktop". Not "the far end", not "the core", not "the original".
      * No internal vocabulary: no note or stage numbers, no class names.
-->
